# HANDOFF — V14 landing site

**Written 2026-09-01, end of the design-QA session. Read this plus `shared/TITLE-TIERS.md` and
`SESSION-2026-08-31.md` before touching anything.**

Designer: Inkyung Choi (Mogo). Works in Korean, replies best to measured numbers rather than
adjectives. Files live on her Mac at `~/Desktop/V14/`, deployed to GitHub Pages. Reference screen is
a MacBook 15" at **1512px** — check that width first, always.

---

## Goal

Polish the "Intelligent Investing" V14 landing site (8 static HTML pages) so that every value on it
is either **on the design system** or **has a recorded reason not to be**. The work is screenshot-
driven: she sends a crop, names what feels wrong, and expects the cause found and fixed sitewide —
never patched in one section only. Her standing instruction:

> "한 섹션만 가능하게 꼼수 부리면 안 되고" — no per-section hacks.

---

## How to work on this (the part that matters most)

1. **Measure before claiming.** Never read a CSS line and report it as the rendered value. Render the
   page headless and read computed styles / rects. Scripts live in the container at `~/v14m/*.py`
   (playwright + chromium). Pattern: stage the HTML, run, print numbers in `u` units.
2. **`u` is the unit.** `--u: calc(100vw / 2545)`. Everything scales from a 2545px Figma frame.
   Report spacing in `u`, not px — px changes with the window and she will (correctly) call it
   meaningless. Rail 1645u, gutter 30u, **column 109.583u**. 6 col = 807.5u, 7 col = 947.08u,
   5 col = 667.9u, 4 col = 528.3u.
3. **Type sizes have floors.** `--t-body: max(17px, 22u)` etc. So a token named `--t-mono15` renders
   **13px** on a laptop. The floored type and the unfloored measures diverge — that divergence is the
   root cause of most bugs found in this project.
4. **Kill the reveal animation before measuring**: add `.in` to every `.rv`/`.ri` and disable
   transitions/animations, or you measure mid-fade. Also `transform:none`.
5. **Measure ink, not boxes**, when the question is "does this look too far apart" — use a `Range`
   over the text nodes. Box gaps lie when font sizes differ.
6. **Inter does not load in the container** (Google Fonts is blocked). Geometry is exact; anything
   font-dependent (character counts, line counts) is an approximation with the fallback face. Say so
   rather than reporting it as fact. Inter's average char width, measured by her on her own machine:
   **0.503em**. chars = (width_px / font_size) / 0.503.
7. **Background images are not staged** unless you stage them. They are ~5MB each; downscale on the
   device with PIL into `_archive/imgproxy/` first, then stage. Without them a photo section renders
   as flat black and you will draw the wrong conclusion.
8. **Cascade traps.** Before concluding "this rule does nothing", grep for a **higher-specificity
   copy** of the same selector. Two that bit this session:
   - `.close9 .cols .ccol .pricehd9` (0,4,0) silently beat `.close9 .pricehd9` (0,2,0).
   - `.acct3 .a h3` mobile: both pages looked identical because the real controller was
     **`shared/v11.css`**, not either page. Grep the shared sheet first.
   - `.acct3 .a p` matches the mono `.lim` first — the card is `h3 / .lim / p / .lim` and the body is
     the **second** `p`. Getting this wrong reports a nonexistent typeset.
9. **Back up before each change**: `cp x.html _archive/x-pre-<topic>-YYYYMMDD.html`. ~45 such files
   exist from 2026-09-01 alone.
10. **`device_bash` cannot delete files.** `rm` fails with "Operation not permitted". Move to a
    `_to_delete/` folder and tell her, or ask for delete permission.
11. Cache-bust `shared/v11.css` separately from the HTML when checking in a real browser.

---

## The design system as it now stands

### Prose measure — THE WHOLE RULE (audited across all 6 content pages, 2026-09-01)

- **A. Prose that OWNS its row:** 6 col at ≥1800, **7 col at ≤1799** → `var(--prose)`
- **B. Prose that SHARES its row** (with a figure, a mockup, or a second prose column):
  **6 col at every width** → the 12-col formula

B never takes the 7-col bump because 7 leaves only 5 columns and every shared row needs more than
that (a 5-col mockup plus a spacer, or a second 6-col prose column). **B is not a per-section
exception.** `.specimens`, `.calgrid`, `.close9 .cols`, `.defgrid`, `.pfgrid`, `.devgrid` are all 6.

Two spellings, one rule: index / self-directed / managed carry `--prose` (a width); pricing /
manifesto / newsroom carry `--prose-cols` (a column count). Consolidating them is unfinished work.

### TYPESET registry — the criterion is ITEM COUNT

| | title / body | tokens |
|---|---|---|
| TYPESET 1 · LARGE | 28 / 500 / 1.25 + 17 / 400 / 1.3 | `--t-h34` + `--t-body` (currently unused) |
| TYPESET 2 · MEDIUM | 22 / 500 / 1.25 + 17 / 400 / 1.3 | `--t-read27` + `--t-body` |
| TYPESET 3 · SMALL | 17 / 500 / 1.25 + 15 / 400 / 1.3 | `--t-body` + `--t-small17` |

**3 items or fewer → TYPESET 2. 4 or more → TYPESET 3.** Tested against all 8 multi-item rows; it is
the only candidate that survives (padding, fill, and column width all fail). Causal: 3 items = 4 col
each ≈ 300px, where 22 fits; 4 items = 3 col ≈ 225px, where 22 breaks badly. `.rows3` (REVIEW) is the
proof it is count and not box-ness — no fill, no side padding, 3 items, TYPESET 2.

Full registry and the per-row table are in `shared/TITLE-TIERS.md`. **She calls these by name**
("typeset 2로 해줘") — apply the table, do not re-derive.

### Spacing scale
14u · 28u · 42u · 71u · 104u · 113u · 184u.
- title → body **14u** (ROW RULES)
- panel padding **42u**; a card/row that is its own panel takes 42u
- prose paragraph → paragraph **24px flat** (deliberately flat, not u — 24 against the 22.1 leading
  is 1.09×, which is the whole point)
- two sentences meant to read as **one** statement: margin **0**, leading only
  (her words: "한문단의 행간처럼")
- section padding 184u top and bottom, verified symmetric

### Mono (IBM Plex Mono)
Ladder **13 / 11 / 9**, tracking `0.04em` everywhere. Leading rule B: multi-line mono prose 1.5,
one-line label/meta 1.4; captions 9px/1.4. Mono = meta only (labels, dates, captions, specs) —
**never prose body**. Price-condition text (`.fee9`) is the **11** tier on mobile on all three pages.
Modifier classes (`.mut`) set colour only; role classes set size and leading.

### Radius
`--r-site:4px` (site boxes, diagram figures) · `--r-app:12px` (app mockups — `.dr-doc`, `.cal-card`)
· `--r-app-in:6px` (boxes inside a mockup) · `--r-pill:99px`.

### Hairlines
Canon **0.667px**. Dark grounds `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)`; light grounds `rgba(28,28,28,0.16)`;
**a dark box on a light ground takes `--c-800`** (the `.dr-doc` answer). Product-UI mockups are
excluded from the hairline sweep and keep their own 1px internal scale (HANDOFF 4-B-7).

### Grounds and fills
- Light-ground panel canon: **white on cream**, 42u, 4px (home membership cards, `.close9 .offer`).
  This is correct — do not "fix" it.
- Dark ground: `--c-1000 #1C1C1C` on black.
- **A mockup on a black ground uses `--c-surface #151515`**, not `--c-elev #0A0A0A` (10/255 off black
  is invisible). Precedent: `.constfig`.
- **The fill answers to its ground**: opaque on a flat ground; **translucent on a photo** so the photo
  reads through. `.refuse .r` = `rgba(28,28,28,0.60)` — measured as the most transparent value that
  keeps the c-200 body at AAA over that photo (see below).
- Status colours: `--c-live-muted #288752` (green/tracking), `--c-review-muted #966E26` (gold/
  sold-early), `--c-urgent-muted #BE3C36` (red), `--c-700` (neutral/void).

### App mockups are one class, one size
`.dr-doc` (memo) and `.cal-card` (record) — the only two app screens. **5 col (667.9u), max-width
566px, radius 12px.** `.constfig`, `.pffig`, `.loopfig` are canvas *diagrams*, a different class
(radius 4px).

### Figure placement
All three figures on self-directed sit on **track 3 of the 6 col / 1fr / 5 col figure grid**:
**5 col wide, left edge at column 7.22**, verified identical at 1920 and 1512. Grids: `.specimens`,
`.calgrid`, and `.close9 .cols.figrow`. When a prose row needs a figure, give it this grid — do not
put the figure in a prose track.

---

## What worked

- **Measure, then decide.** Every value she accepted was derived from a measurement, not proposed.
  Two examples worth copying:
  - *Card transparency*: composited c-1000 over the actual photo at the actual card region,
    p99.99 worst case, contrast against c-200 → alpha 0.60 (7.9:1, AAA). It also **killed the
    "outline only" option with data** (no fill = 3.8:1, a WCAG failure) instead of by opinion.
  - *"The photo is too dark"*: the histogram said it was not — its midtone (26.8) was **higher** than
    the accepted photo's (7.7). Its **range** was 17.4 vs 28–80 for every other photo. So the fix was
    contrast, not brightness, and it applied to exactly one photo.
- **Find the site's own precedent before inventing a value.** `--c-surface` for a mockup on black,
  `--c-800` for a dark box on a light ground, `box-decoration-break:clone` for per-line plates — all
  three already existed elsewhere in the codebase for the same situation.
- **Subtracting beats retuning.** The constellation's 30-label rim ring was removed after thinning it
  to 12 made it worse. Own the failed attempt in the comment.
- **Write the reasoning into the CSS comment**, including reversals and what was tried and rejected.
  The codebase's comments are load-bearing documentation and she reads them.

## What didn't work

- **Reporting a CSS line as the rendered value.** Claimed `.acct3 .a h3` differed between two pages
  from reading source; measurement showed both were already identical and the real controller was the
  shared sheet. Always render.
- **`box-decoration-break:clone` on a flex item.** A flex item blockifies `display:inline`, so the
  clone never applies. Retracted once, then solved by putting the plate on an inline **child**
  (`.hero .hbar .hp`).
- **Thinning the rim labels to 12 at 9px** — worse than 30 at 6.5px. The ring's radius (~37px) cannot
  hold twelve ~90px strings at any legible size.
- **`contrast()` above 1 on a dark image** — it pivots on 0.5, so it crushes everything to black.
  Brightness must return to 1 first.
- **Subgrid `grid-row: span N` where N < the flow-child count** — the overflow stacks silently into
  the last track and prints on top of the previous item. Count the children first.
- **Guessing an alpha / a filter / a gap by eye.** Every one of these got sent back until measured.

